en-US.diagram-studio.usage:
**What it does**: a structured diagram studio — four diagram types render differently (shapes / colors / auto-layout), with an interactive canvas inside the plugin page (drag, connect, edit labels, restyle nodes with shapes & colors, undo/redo, one-click auto-layout, PNG export) plus a drawing API the agent drives from chat; mermaid blocks in documents convert to an editable canvas in one click ("To canvas"); nodes can link to knowledge-base documents (click the badge to jump), diagrams generate ordering / fill-in-the-blank questions deterministically into the review loop, support blank-out recall practice (active recall on the document's SM-2 schedule), and live as knowledge-base documents exporting to mermaid.

**How to use**:
1. Sidebar "Diagram Studio" → New Diagram (pick a type) → click a row to open the canvas (drag / connect / double-click to edit, select a node to restyle or link a document, Ctrl+Z to undo, auto-layout to tidy, export PNG; save writes back to the document);
2. Tell Baize "Draw a login flow: enter account → validate → home", it calls the drawing API step by step (with shapes & colors) and lays it out automatically;
3. Tell Baize "Turn this document into a mindmap", then keep hand-tuning;
4. In the document preview, click "To canvas" at the top-right of a mermaid block (or tell Baize "convert this document's diagrams to canvas") — the mermaid block becomes an editable canvas diagram;
5. Select a node on the canvas and "Link doc…" to chain it to a knowledge-base document (click the 📄 badge to jump; dangling links can be unlinked in one click); tell Baize "make questions from this diagram" to deterministically generate ordering / fill-in-the-blank questions into review;
6. Click the "Recall" row action (or the "Recall" toolbar button on the canvas): the canvas blanks out some nodes by connectivity — fill them from memory and submit for per-blank grading; false negatives can be fixed with "Mark correct", and answers advance the diagram document's SM-2 review schedule (tree ⏰ and tray nudges follow for free). You can also tell Baize "recall this diagram".

**When to use**: mapping processes and architecture, sketching before studying, drawing deployment diagrams in review, turning diagrams into practice, blank-out recall for active review.

**Notes**: diagram generation uses the current Agent model (consumes quota); mermaid-to-canvas, diagram-to-questions, and recall projection/grading are local deterministic transforms (zero model calls; mermaid supports the flowchart/graph TD|LR subset); question banking requires the "Practice" plugin (declined honestly when absent); recall attempts feed the document review schedule and never enter the question bank; every write passes the platform shared-kernel validation — invalid diagrams are never saved.

